  recipeId: led
  concept: 'Authored objective: Green LED Conducting.

    Authored requirement:
    Green LED must be forward biased and conducting. Assign fixed ID LED2 to its
    SparkLED component. Connection pair led_2_Anode and led_2_Cathode. Conduction
    required.

    General teaching principle: An LED has a defined anode and cathode;
    correct polarity and suitable current control matter for normal forward operation.

    Only
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
